WEBVTT

00:05:59.397 --> 00:06:01.194
and threw it at the speaker.

00:06:01.218 --> 00:06:03.815
So let me tell you what I'm going to do.

00:06:03.839 --> 00:06:07.708
I've asked the people sitting
in the tables right next to the stage

00:06:07.732 --> 00:06:09.626
to serve as my human shield."

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:10.906
AG: And it worked!

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:13.017
ME: And I ended up
speaking for 40 minutes,

00:06:13.041 --> 00:06:15.116
and there were lots of questions.

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:18.110
Can you tell, I still remember
it vividly? (Chuckles)

00:06:18.134 --> 00:06:21.556
AG: Why did Mohamed's authenticity
resonate with the audience?

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:26.406
Classic and recent experiments suggest
that showing vulnerability humanizes you,

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:28.688
and people tend to like that.

00:06:28.712 --> 00:06:31.053
But there's a crucial caveat: